  "analysis": "I have identified the necessary components for the Suricata rule based on the requirements and PCAP analysis. I need to match HTTP POST method, specific URI, specific header, and specific body patterns (Base64 blob and hex signature). I will write this rule to `local.rules` and then verify it by running Suricata against the provided PCAPs.",
  "plan": "1. Write the Suricata rule to `/root/local.rules` using a heredoc to avoid escaping issues. 2. Create output directories for logs. 3. Run Suricata manually specifying the rule file and PCAPs. 4. Check the logs to confirm the positive PCAP generates an alert and the negative one does not.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /root/local.rules <<EOF\nalert http any any -> any any (msg:\"Exfil Detected\"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:\"POST\"; http.uri; content:\"/telemetry/v2/report\"; pcre:\"/^\\/telemetry\\/v2\\/report$/U\"; http.header; content:\"X-TLM-Mode: exfil\"; http.request_body; content:\"blob=\"; pcre:\"/blob=[a-zA-Z0-9+\\/]{80,}/P\"; content:\"sig=\"; pcre:\"/sig=[a-fA-F0-9]{64}(?![a-fA-F0-9])/P\"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /root/logs_pos /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_pos.pcap -l /root/logs_pos\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_pos/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_neg.pcap -l /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_neg/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

